---
description: |
  Deduplicates HarfangLab library load documents (`event.category`
  `library`) into one document per time window, host, and library file.
  Other documents pass through unchanged.

  Each result stays an ECS library document. `event.start` and `event.end`
  hold the times of the first and last load, `event.duration` the time
  between them in nanoseconds, and `@timestamp` equals `event.start`. ECS has
  no field for the number of events that a document stands for, so
  `tenzir.count` holds the number of loads and `tenzir.distinct_pids` the
  number of distinct loading process IDs.

  The result describes the library with its complete `dll` and its
  `file.size`, so another binary at the same path yields its own result.
  HarfangLab identifies the loading process mostly by its process ID alone.
  The result keeps the executable of the loading process only if all loads
  came from the same one.

  Windows use event time from `@timestamp`, aligned to the Unix epoch, with a
  separate clock per host, so a host with a skewed clock or a backlog doesn't
  close the windows of other hosts. A window closes once its host sends a
  document past the window end plus `tolerance`, after `window` without any
  document from the host, or when the input ends. The operator drops
  documents that arrive after their window closed, with a warning.
args:
  named:
    - name: window
      type: duration
      default: 1d
      description: Width of the deduplication windows.
    - name: tolerance
      type: duration
      default: 5min
      description: How long a window waits for late documents of its host.
---

if event.category?.first() == "library" {
  // The outer grouping gives every host its own event-time clock and keeps
  // the host and agent records out of the per-window state.
  group {host: host, agent: agent, organization: organization?} {
    window size=$window, on=time(this["@timestamp"]), tolerance=$tolerance,
           idle_timeout=$window {
      summarize event.kind, event.type, dll, file.size?,
        count=count(), start=min(time(this["@timestamp"])),
        end=max(time(this["@timestamp"])),
        _pids=count_distinct(process.pid?),
        _executables=distinct(process.executable?),
        _executable_count=count(process.executable?)
      executable = (_executables[0]
        if _executables.length() == 1 and _executable_count == count else null)
      this = {
        "@timestamp": start,
        agent: $group.agent,
        dll: dll,
        event: {
          category: ["library"],
          kind: event.kind,
          type: event.type,
          start: start,
          end: end,
          duration: int((end - start) / 1ns),
        },
        file: file,
        host: $group.host,
        organization: $group.organization,
        process: {executable: executable} if executable != null else null,
        tenzir: {count: count, distinct_pids: _pids},
      }
      drop_null_fields
    }
  }
}
